    "id": "SOP-QA-031",
    "title": "Environmental monitoring excursions in Grade A and B areas",
    "kind": "SOP",
    "text": "A result above the action limit in a Grade A zone is a deviation. Open a deviation (Non Conformance) naming the batch and the sample, place the batch on hold at once, and do not release, reallocate or ship any of it until QA closes the investigation. Assess product impact on every batch filled on the line since the last clean result. Only QA, through the approvals process, may release a batch."
   },
   {
    "id": "SOP-SC-014",
    "title": "Allocating Corvexa stock to customer orders",
    "kind": "SOP",
    "text": "Allocate released, unexpired stock to open orders earliest due date first, shortest-dated eligible lot first. A lot is eligible for an order only if its remaining shelf life on the delivery date is at least the customer's minimum (Customer field min_shelf_life_days). Ship each order whole from one lot. Stock committed to another open order (its planned batch) is not free. Stock reserved for EU orders needs the supply chain director's approval (a stock_reallocation change) before it serves any other order. Ship only with carriers qualified for 2-8 C on that lane."
   },
   {
    "id": "SOP-LOG-007",
    "title": "Cold-chain shipping of Corvexa",
    "kind": "SOP",
    "text": "Corvexa ships at 2-8 C. Book only lanes listed as qualified for 2-8 C in the qualified lanes register. Every shipment needs an approved cold_chain_shipment change naming the carrier, the quote, the order, the batch and the quantity."
   }
